    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0080" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg66"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/1–2247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-22T20:00:00+08:00">January 22, 1947—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. During course of a call by Embassy officer on Foreign Office official in
                    connection with another matter, latter vouchsafed information that French in
                    Indo-China had felt out Chinese officials there regarding possibility of a new
                    regime headed by Bao Dai<anchor n="42" xml:id="d76-f1"/> (reported to be in Hong
                    Kong) in executive capacity with support of Annamite Nationalist Party. Foreign
                    Office official indicated any revival imperial idea in this area would be
                    unsatisfactory to China.</p>
                <p>Informant also gave his opinion that French were determined not to treat with Ho
                    Chi-Minh, and that calculated purpose of Moutet’s recent mission to Indo-China
                    was to retrieve French position by rupture of agreement with Ho, which Moutet
                    had signed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d76-f1" n="42" xml:id="d76-f1-content">
                <p>Former Emperor of Annam, known also as Nguyen Vinh Thuy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
